e that. First, divide 168 by 840. Hmm, 840 divided by 168. Let me see, 168 times 5 is 840. So, 168 divided by 840 is 0.2. Then, multiplying by 100 gives 20%. So, the combined remoras make up 20% of the dolphin's body length.\n\nWait, let me double-check that. If the dolphin is 70 feet long, which is 840 inches, and the remoras are 84 inches each, two of them would be 168 inches. So, 168 divided by 840 is indeed 0.2, which is 20%. That seems right. Let me confirm with another method. If 168 inches is 20% of 840 inches, then 10% would be 84 inches, so 20% would be 168 inches. Yep, that checks out. So, the answer should be 20%.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe combined length of the remoras is \\boxed{20\\%} of the dolphin's body length.\n</think>\n\nTo determine the percentage of the dolphin's body length that is the combined length of the remoras, we first convert the dolphin's body length from feet to inches. \n\nThe dolphin's body length is 70 feet, which converts to:\n\\[\n70 \\text{ feet} \\times 12 \\text{ inches/foot} = 840 \\text{ inches}\n\\]\n\nEach remora is 84 inches, and there are 2 remoras. The combined length of the remoras is:\n\\[\n2 \\times 84 \\text{ inches} = 168 \\text{ inches}\n\\]\n\nTo find the percentage of the dolphin's body length that is the combined remoras, we use the formula for percentage:\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{168 \\text{ inches}}{840 \\text{ inches}} \\right) \\times 100 = 0.2 \\times 100 = 20\\%\n\\]\n\nThus, the combined length of the remoras is \\boxed{20\\%} of the dolphin's body length.", "model_answer": 20.0, "ground_truth": 20.0, "is_correct": true}
