over 57 miles? But that would be a different interpretation. Wait, but the problem says \"It takes 152 minutes to cover every 19 miles of the city.\" So, that is, the entire 19 miles is covered in 152 minutes. So, the rate is 19 miles per 152 minutes. So, the time to cover 57 miles would be 57 divided by (19/152). So, 57*(152/19)=456. So, that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, if the problem had said that the fogbank covers 19 miles in 152 minutes, and the city is 57 miles wide, then the time to cover the city would be (57/19)*152 minutes. So, same as before.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the problem is about the entire city being covered, so the front of the fogbank has to move 57 miles. If the front moves at 19 miles per 152 minutes, then time is 57/(19/152)=456 minutes. So, same answer.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the problem is about the entire city being covered, so the entire 57 miles. If the fog is moving at a rate of 19 miles per 152 minutes, then the time to cover 57 miles is (57/19)*152 minutes. So, 3*152=456. So, same answer.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the problem is about the entire city being covered, so the time is (57 miles)/( (19 miles / 152 minutes) ). So, 57/(19/152)=57*(152/19)=456. So, same answer.\n\nSo, all different ways of approaching the problem lead to 456 minutes. Therefore, the answer is 456", "model_answer": 456.0, "ground_truth": 456.0, "is_correct": true}
