ire yield. So in a year, he can harvest twice. Therefore, total harvest is 4970*2=9940. That seems right.\n\nAlternatively, if the 71 apricots per square meter is per 6 months, then in 6 months, he would harvest 71*70*6=29820 apricots, and then in the next 6 months another 29820, totaling 59640. But the problem states \"There are 71 apricots per square meter.\" It doesn't specify per season or per year. Generally, when such problems mention yield per unit area, it's per year unless specified otherwise. So I think the first approach is correct. So 70*71=4970 per year, and since he can harvest every 6 months, he can do that twice a year, so 4970*2=9940.\n\nBut let me check again. Let's parse the problem statement again: \"Yuki has 70 square meters of apricot field. There are 71 apricots per square meter. Yuki can harvest his apricots every 6 months. How many apricots can Yuki harvest within a year?\"\n\nSo \"There are 71 apricots per square meter\" – that's the yield. So each square meter produces 71 apricots in total. So over a year, each square meter gives 71 apricots. Therefore, 70 square meters give 70*71=4970 apricots per year. Then, \"Yuki can harvest his apricots every 6 months.\" So every 6 months, he can harvest all the apricots that have ripened. So in a year, which is two 6-month periods, he can harvest twice. Therefore, total harvest is 4970*2=9940.\n\nAlternatively, if the 71 apricots per square meter is per 6-month period, then in each 6 months he would get 71*70=4970 apricots, and then in the next 6 months another 4970, totaling 9940. Wait, that's the same answer. Wait, so whether the 71 is per year or per 6 months, if he can harvest every 6 months, then in each 6 months he gets 71*70=4970, so two times would be 9940. So maybe that's the answer.\n\nBut the problem says \"There are 71 apricots per square meter.\" If that's per year, then 70*71=4970 per year. If that's per 6 months, then 70*71*2=9940 per year. But the problem doesn't specify. Hmm. This is