\n\n1. **Water used for giant cubes**: \n   \\[\n   8 \\text{ cubes} \\times 13 \\text{ ounces per cube} = 104 \\text{ ounces}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Water used for medium cubes**: \n   \\[\n   13 \\text{ cubes} \\times 12 \\text{ ounces per cube} = 156 \\text{ ounces}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Water used for small cubes**: \n   \\[\n   24 \\text{ cubes} \\times \\frac{1}{3} \\text{ ounce per cube} = 8 \\text{ ounces}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Total water used**: \n   \\[\n   104 \\text{ ounces} + 156 \\text{ ounces} + 8 \\text{ ounces} = 268 \\text{ ounces}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Water left**: \n   \\[\n   346 \\text{ ounces} - 268 \\text{ ounces} = 78 \\text{ ounces}\n   \\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{78}\n\\]", "model_answer": 78.0, "ground_truth": 78.0, "is_correct": true}
