\nThe number of bananas Thiago won't be able to place on the baskets is \\boxed{49}.\n</think>\n\nThiago places bananas on 8 baskets, each holding 20 bananas. To find out how many bananas he can't place, we first calculate the total number of bananas that can be placed on the baskets:\n\n\\[\n8 \\text{ baskets} \\times 20 \\text{ bananas per basket} = 160 \\text{ bananas}\n\\]\n\nThiago has 209 bananas in total. Subtracting the number of bananas that can be placed from the total number of bananas gives:\n\n\\[\n209 \\text{ bananas} - 160 \\text{ bananas} = 49 \\text{ bananas}\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of bananas Thiago won't be able to place on the baskets is \\(\\boxed{49}\\).", "model_answer": 49.0, "ground_truth": 49.0, "is_correct": true}
