apacity. So, the number of olives that won't fit is 1. \n\n**Final Answer**\nThe number of olives Ibrahim won't be able to place on the plates is \\boxed{1}.\n</think>\n\nIbrahim has 321 olives and 10 plates, each capable of holding 32 olives. To find out how many olives he won't be able to place, we first calculate the total capacity of the plates:\n\n\\[\n32 \\text{ olives/plate} \\times 10 \\text{ plates} = 320 \\text{ olives}\n\\]\n\nNext, we subtract the total capacity from the total number of olives he has:\n\n\\[\n321 \\text{ olives} - 320 \\text{ olives} = 1 \\text{ olive}\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of olives Ibrahim won't be able to place on the plates is \\boxed{1}.", "model_answer": 1.0, "ground_truth": 1.0, "is_correct": true}
