e number of ledges:\n\n\\[\n11 \\times 69 = 759\n\\]\n\nShe is going to give 4 potted plants from each ledge to friends and family. To find the total number of plants given away, we multiply the number of plants per ledge by the number of ledges:\n\n\\[\n4 \\times 69 = 276\n\\]\n\nSubtracting the number of plants given away from the total number of plants she currently has:\n\n\\[\n759 - 276 = 483\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of potted plants Sakura will remain with is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{483}\n\\]", "model_answer": 483.0, "ground_truth": 521.0, "is_correct": false}
